==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|highway-robbery}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|highway|robbery|lang=en}}. Compare {{cog|ang|weġrēaf||highway robbery|lit=road-theft}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|highway robberies}}

# {{lb|en|literally|historical}} The act of [[rob]]bing a [[traveler]] on a public road.
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} Said of [[excessive]] or [[exorbitant]] prices.
#: ''They think they can charge $400 for a shirt? That's '''highway robbery'''.''

====Synonyms====
{{sense|the asking of an excessive or exorbitant price}} [[daylight robbery]]

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|bargain}}, {{l|en|steal}}

